1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[Kurapika] They're coming.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
They are definitely coming!

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
[theme song playing]

4
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
DEFEND x AND x ATTACK

5
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
[narrator] September 1st.

6
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The day Gon, Killua, Kurapika and Leorio

7
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,000
have chosen to reunite in Yorknew City.

8
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,000
And it is on this morning
that Gon and Killua

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
visit the bustling Yorknew marketplace.

10
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
[Gon] Wow, look at all the people!

11
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,000
[Killua] The whole purpose of this market

12
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
is to swindle the visitors
who’ve come for the auction.

13
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
[Gon] Wait.
So, this isn’t the auction venue?

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,000
No, of course it isn’t.

15
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Yorknew’s “dream auction”
is held once a year

16
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
in the world’s largest auction house.

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
They say that tens of trillions of Jenny

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,000
exchange hands during only ten days
of official bidding.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Tens of trillions? Really?

20
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Yeah. Something
that sells for 10,000 today

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
could go for a hundred million tomorrow.

22
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Bam, instant fortune.

23
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
It’s where dreams come true.

24
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
[Gon] Wow...

25
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,000
[Killua] Well, anyway,

26
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
that’s a big part of the reason
why so much of the underworld auctioning

27
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
happens at the same time.

28
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[Gon] That’s awesome!

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[Killua] So hey, you think
Kurapika and Leorio are gonna show?

30
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
[Gon] They promised
they’d meet us here today,

31
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
so I’m sure they will.

32
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
[Killua] Right.

33
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
They might try to contact us, so...

34
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Gon! You’ve really gotta get a phone!

35
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Every Hunter needs one!

36
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Yeah. I know...

37
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
[shop owner] Hey, welcome!

38
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
This one’s the hottest new models.

39
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
It’s ultra-thin and no bigger
than a credit card!

40
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Plus, it has GPS,
which is great for finding people.

41
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
-[Leorio] Don't bother.
-[Gon and Killua] Huh?

42
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
The range is terrible
and it’s not even waterproof.

43
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
The only thing it’s good for
is making phone calls.

44
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Leorio!

45
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Hey!

46
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Instead, I would recommend...

47
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
this Beetle 07.

48
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
It’s pretty heavy and expensive

49
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
but it can translate over 200 languages

50
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
from places all around the globe.

51
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Wait, Really?

52
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
-Hey, get this one and I’ll get one, too!
-[Gon] Yeah!

53
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Two of these beauties, please!

54
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Yes sir, that’ll be 400,000.

55
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,000
[screams] Four hundred--

56
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:36,000
That’s highway robbery!

57
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
[Gon] Thanks, Leorio!

58
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
[Leorio]
Sure, but a 110,580 Jenny apiece?

59
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
And that’s a fair price for a new model
in this market!

60
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:48,000
[Killua] Still, you overdid it.

61
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:52,000
I’ve never seen anyone get applause
for buying a cell phone before.

62
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
-[applause]
-[Leorio whistling]

63
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
[Gon] But you really saved us.

64
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
[Leorio] That was just a taste
of what I’m capable of.

65
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:04,000
The real deals don’t really start rolling
until after the seller asks you to leave.

66
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
[overconfident laughter]

67
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,000
He doesn’t really strike me
as the auction-going type.

68
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
No kidding.

69
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
So. How you coming along?

70
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
What do you mean?

71
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
You’ve both been training
and getting stronger, haven’t you?

72
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
[Killua snorts]

73
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,000
What?

74
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,000
You gave the badge
back to Hisoka at Heavens Arena?!

75
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Not to mention you were good enough
to reach the 200th floor…

76
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Just how strong have you gotten?

77
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[Gon] Hey. Did you learn Nen, Leorio?

78
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
You better believe I did.

79
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
That’s awesome!

80
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Seriously?

81
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Why the hell would I lie about that?

82
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:42,000
It’s building up a shroud of aura,

83
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
making your own life force even stronger!

84
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
[disappointed groan]

85
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
That’s Ten, actually.

86
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
One of the four major principles
for learning Nen.

87
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
What?! Are you saying there’s more to it?

88
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
I figured it’d be something like that.

89
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
[Leorio] Greed Island?
What’s that?

90
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
A legendary game.

91
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
[Gon] We're trying to get a copy
at the auction.

92
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
But why would you even want one?

93
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,000
I think the game

94
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
might have a clue in it
that’ll help me find my dad.

95
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Huh? A clue hidden in some video game?

96
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Why d’you think that?

97
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[Gon] It’s... kind of a long story.

98
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
[Killua] Anyway, the problem’s the cost.

99
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,000
How much is it?

100
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[Killua] The lowest starting bid...

101
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
is 8.9 billion.

102
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Did you say billion?!

103
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,000
And how much do you have?

104
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
[sheepish chuckle]

105
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,000
After some bad investments
we’re down to... five million.

106
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Okay, guys, listen up.

107
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,000
This event is being held at Southernbees,

108
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,000
the world’s finest auction house,

109
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
so that much money
won’t even cover the entry fee.

110
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
But the acquisition rank for the game

111
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
was listed as “easy”
on the Hunter website.

112
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Really?

113
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:51,000
[Gon] Because to get your hands on a copy,

114
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
all you need is money.

115
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,000
[laughs] It’s like I always say,
money makes the world go round!

116
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
-[Killua] Well...
-[both] Hm?

117
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
All that really means...

118
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
is that a real treasure
can’t just be purchased.

119
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:06,000
If you can’t get one,
and pretty easily, too,

120
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
you’re not much of a Hunter.

121
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
Right, you guys?

122
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
[miffed grunts]

123
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[Leorio snorts]
I don’t need you to tell me that.

124
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:17,000
First things first,
we need some seed money.

125
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Something to get the ball rolling.

126
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,000
Let’s search for ways
we can make fast cash in Yorknew!

127
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,000
[Gon] Yeah!

128
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[Killua] Simple and stupid.

129
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
He must be an Enhancer, too.

130
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
[Milluki] Dammit. What’s wrong?!

131
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
I created a complete duplicate
of the program.

132
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
So why aren’t any events being triggered?

133
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Did Kil trick me?

134
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
No. No, there’s no way!

135
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
He doesn’t have the skills
to forge a game

136
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,000
and he’s definitely not stupid enough
to double cross me!

137
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
So, either he was tricked too,

138
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
or this is the real deal!

139
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
I have to know.

140
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
I’ll find out its secret,
whatever it takes…

141
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
no matter what the cost!

142
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,000
I’ve got 12.7 billion left.

143
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
And I’m gonna need
at least twice that amount

144
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
to guarantee a winning bid.

145
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Dad! I want to make a deal.

146
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Lend me 15 billion
and I’ll kill 15 people.

147
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Got it. Bye.

148
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
[Blimp] Autopilot engaged
to Lingon Airport.

149
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:26,000
[Milluki] I think I was
about ten years old…

150
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
the last time I left the house.

151
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
[Leorio] Huh? Swap?

152
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
[Gon] What does that mean?

153
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
[computer] “Swap meet:

154
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
A gathering for the auction
and barter of objects.”

155
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
See also: Conditional Auction.

156
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Conditional auction?

157
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,000
[computer] “Conditional auction:

158
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:50,000
An exchange in which the seller
specifies a non-monetary condition

159
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,000
and hands the item over to the first buyer
who satisfies that condition.

160
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
-Conditions, huh?
-What does that mean?

161
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
All right...

162
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
I think I get it.

163
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
So, there’s another kind of auctioning!

164
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
[cackling]

165
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Dalzollene] At 9:00 tonight,
the mummy of Princess Corco

166
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
will be sold off
at the Underground Auction.

167
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
Ivlenkov, Tocino and Baise,

168
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
you’ll be responsible for the bidding.

169
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[Basho] Are three people gonna be enough?

170
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
[Dalzollene] Buyers can only enter
in groups of three.

171
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
Weapons, communication,
and recording devices

172
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
are all strictly forbidden.

173
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
The Mafia that runs
the Underground Auction

174
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,000
also handles security,

175
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
so there’s rarely any trouble.

176
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
All it takes is one miscalculated move

177
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
and then every Mafia member in the world

178
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
becomes your enemy.

179
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
This auction is built
on a foundation of trust.

180
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
And that’s the reason

181
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
you won’t see
any surveillance cameras on-site.

182
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
The one unspoken rule

183
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
is that any grudges
are to be checked at the door.

184
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,000
And so, if anything does happen,

185
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,000
your word is of utmost importance.

186
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
There are no courts here,

187
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
but it will hold the same weight
as sworn testimony.

188
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
It’s crucial that each one of you
makes a glowing impression.

189
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Don’t cause minor disturbances
for any reason.

190
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Speak to no one outside of this group.

191
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
And... The rest of us?

192
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:21,000
[Dalzollene] Basho and Linssen will be
covering the rear entrance.

193
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Kurapika and Melody
will take the front entrance.

194
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Squala and I will guard the girl.

195
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,000
And so...

196
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:32,000
the mission will now begin.

197
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,000
[Leorio] Step right up, folks!

198
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Let’s have a little
conditional auctioning fun!

199
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Here’s what’s up for bid!

200
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
A diamond worth three million!

201
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
Bought today
with a certificate of authenticity!

202
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Arm wrestling decides the winner!

203
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
First person to beat this boy walks off
with the diamond!

204
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Entry fee is ten thousand!

205
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
All right. The auction starts now!

206
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
-I want in on that!
-Me, too!

207
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[man] Same here!

208
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:09,000
[Leorio] No pushing, people!

209
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Form a line.

210
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Adjust your strength to match
that of your opponent.

211
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,000
And pretend to struggle
every now and then.

212
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
-Okay, you’re up first!
-[gasps]

213
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
[Leorio] The entry fee in advance, please.

214
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Here ya go. Ten thousand.

215
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,000
Thank you, sir. Now step right up!

216
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
[grunts]

217
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
[Leorio] All right, clasp hands.

218
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Just do what I told you.

219
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,000
[Gon grunts]

220
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
And remember...

221
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:40,000
you get one round!

222
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Ready... Go!

223
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
[both straining]

224
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,000
[Leorio] Uh-oh!

225
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
-Can he do it?
-[Gon straining]

226
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
You’re almost there.

227
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
Don’t give up now!

228
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
[fake straining]

229
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
[roaring]

230
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
[straining]

231
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Oh! That was a close one!

232
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:20,000
Ah, dammit! I lost to a little kid!

233
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
And who will be our next contender?

234
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,000
Ready... and go!

235
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:28,000
[crowd cheering and hooting]

236
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
[Killua] I get it.

237
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,000
So, this is conditional auctioning.

238
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
But to reach 8.9 billion,

239
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,000
we’ll need 889,999 wins.

240
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
[man] Ah, damn.

241
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
Another loser!

242
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
So, who’s up next?

243
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
You lose!

244
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:51,000
[murmuring]

245
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
[onlooker 1] He's beaten 150 people!

246
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
[onlooker 2]
He’s gotta be running out of steam.

247
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
[onlooker 3]
He looks tired and he’s sweating bullets.

248
00:11:58,000 --> 00:11:59,000
[onlooker 4]
Don’t lose before I get my turn!

249
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
[Gon] I feel bad for tricking everybody.

250
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
Making so much money this easily...

251
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
I’m breaking out in a cold sweat
just thinking about it!

252
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Okay! So, who’s up next?

253
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,000
Look at that!

254
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:18,000
We have our first female challenger!

255
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,000
[onlooker 1] All right! Get him, girl!

256
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
[onlooker 2] And try to take it easy
on the little lady, muscle boy!

257
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
So, tell us where you’re from!

258
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,000
All business, I see...

259
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:31,000
-I look forward to our match.
-[Gon] Oh. Yeah, same here.

260
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
[gasps]

261
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Ready, and... go!

262
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:43,000
[Gon and girl straining]

263
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
[Gon straining severely]

264
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
[straining]

265
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Oh! So close! Better luck next time!

266
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Yeah, good effort, girl!

267
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Thank you for the opportunity.

268
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Oh. You’re welcome. Any time.

269
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
[sighs] What a pity.

270
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Was that... full power?

271
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,000
Yeah.

272
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
I wonder who she is...

273
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:31,000
[Killua]
World champion arm wrestler, maybe?

274
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
[Franklin] Well?

275
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
[girl] I lost.

276
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
He’s tough.

277
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
[Feitan] That little brat?

278
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
I sort of wanted that diamond.

279
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Then you shoulda used your left hand.

280
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[Feitan] Yeah, why didn’t you use
your stronger arm?

281
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Oh. Because...

282
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
he extended his right hand first...

283
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
I think I’d like to challenge him again.

284
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
[Feitan] There is no time.

285
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
We have a job to do.

286
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
[Franklin] He’s right.

287
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Besides, buying and bidding’s
not our style.

288
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
We’re thieves, remember?

289
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
[Feitan] If we want something, we take it.

290
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
[Neon] No way!

291
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
I'm going!

292
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,000
-[bawling]
-[grunts]

293
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[Dalzollene] Hear that, Sir?
I’m at a loss here!

294
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
[Dalzollene] Yes, sir.

295
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Her tantrum--

296
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Her crying exhausted her.

297
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
That’s right, she’s fast asleep now, sir.

298
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
But there’s simply no telling
what we’re all in for

299
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
when she finally wakes up again.

300
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
I vow to obtain the items
she wants, but...

301
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
she’s set
on participating in the bidding herself.

302
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
She’s bound to be disappointed
when she wakes up to find

303
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
that she missed her only chance
at doing so.

304
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
[Nostrade] Very well.

305
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I’ll adjust my schedule and head over.

306
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:58,000
For now, focus on getting
the mummy of that princess,

307
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
so we can improve her mood again.

308
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,000
[Dalzollene] Understood, sir.

309
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
[Dalzollene sighs]

310
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[dialing number]

311
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,000
Well? How are things with you?

312
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,000
[Melody] All clear.

313
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
There’s Nothing from the outside.

314
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Yes, sir.

315
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
We’ll call you if anything new happens.

316
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,000
[siren wailing]

317
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
[Melody]
They’re being quite thorough, aren’t they?

318
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:25,000
No one is allowed
within 500 meters of the auction house,

319
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
except for approved
Mafia security personnel.

320
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[Kurapika] If they didn't do that,

321
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:33,000
the perimeter
would be crawling with thugs,

322
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:38,000
which would practically be an announcement
that sinister deeds are taking place.

323
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,000
[Melody] Guess so.

324
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[Kurapika] I wonder...

325
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
will the Phantom Troupe really show up?

326
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,000
[gasps]

327
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
[Melody]
That’s the same sound I heard earlier.

328
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Hmm?

329
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Just so you know,

330
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
I happened to see you
as you were leaving the Hunter agency.

331
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
I heard it when you walked past me.

332
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Your heart played a melody of wrath.

333
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Mind if I ask you a question?

334
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[Kurapika] Go ahead.

335
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
-Scarlet Eyes.
-[light gasp]

336
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Exactly...

337
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
what do they mean to you?

338
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:30,000
[siren wailing]

339
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Why do you ask?

340
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,000
There’s no reason in particular.

341
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Just curious.

342
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
When you saw the image on the data card,

343
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:44,000
your heartbeat was even more fearsome
than it was then.

344
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:49,000
It played a melody of boundless fury.

345
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:56,000
I guess there’s no point in lying.

346
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
I am a member of the Kurta Clan.

347
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Our eyes are normally brown,

348
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:06,000
but they burn a bright crimson
when we’re agitated.

349
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:10,000
So, I wear black contact lenses
to escape detection.

350
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:14,000
I seek the eyes
that were stolen from my brethren.

351
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
And whatever it takes...

352
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
I will return their eyes to them.

353
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:22,000
[Melody] Hmm...

354
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Will you tell Dalzollene about me?

355
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
No, I won’t.

356
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Because you’d kill me if I did.

357
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:33,000
You’re very perceptive.

358
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
A heartbeat’s always honest.

359
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
When you first began confessing,

360
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
and told me your true nature,

361
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,000
your heartbeat was as calm as it was icy.

362
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
The heartbeat of one who is prepared...

363
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,000
to kill if need be.

364
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Your heart says you hold no grudges

365
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
but that I was fair game if I talked.

366
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[Kurapika] Why did you take this job?

367
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,000
[Melody] Why would you ask?

368
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,000
You know that I’ll probably lie to you.

369
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Your eyes will tell me if you do.

370
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
[Melody] I’m also a Pro Hunter.

371
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
A Music Hunter, I suppose.

372
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
I seek a certain sheet music.

373
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[Kurapika] You aren't lying,

374
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,000
but you left out crucial details.

375
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
[Melody giggles]

376
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,000
[Melody] Let’s say you’re right
and leave it at that.

377
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
It’s the Sonata of Darkness.

378
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
That’s what I’m after.

379
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
It is said to be composed
by the devil himself.

380
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:53,000
There are solo parts for the piano,
violin, flute, and harp.

381
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:57,000
If a human plays
or even listens to the piece,

382
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
they will be horribly cursed.

383
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Isn’t that just an urban legend?

384
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
I doubt that anything like that
could truly exist.

385
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
[wind rustles]

386
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:16,000
[Kurapika gasps]

387
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,000
The only solo I heard was the flute solo.

388
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
One movement turned me
into what you see now.

389
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,000
My friend who played it died,

390
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
and her whole body turned to this.

391
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Just a single movement

392
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
from someone who had given warnings

393
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
never to play it under any circumstances.

394
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
That day...

395
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,000
we were drunk and giddy.

396
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:46,000
My body was destroyed,

397
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:49,000
but I gained this ability in return.

398
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,000
I wish to restore my body
to the way it was.

399
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
I’m willing to do anything.

400
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
I don’t want anyone else
to suffer the same fate as me.

401
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
That’s why I want to find the score

402
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
and destroy it.

403
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
You asked me why I took this job.

404
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
The answer is I was hoping

405
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
one devil would know another.

406
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,000
[sighs]

407
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
Looks like it’s time.

408
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:20,000
The Underworld Auction is about to begin.

409
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:26,000
It’s almost time.

410
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,000
It is.

411
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:38,000
[narrator] The Phantom Troupe prepares
to bare its fangs.

412
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:43,000
And soon Kurapika, now a bodyguard
for the Nostrade family,

413
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
must decide on how to deal with them.

414
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[theme song playing]

415
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[Gon] Coming up:

416
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:59,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

417
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

418
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

419
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

420
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
Today, we're introducing Basho!

421
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:08,000
He writes a lot of haiku,
his homeland’s poetry.

422
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
-Let me do one!
-[gasps]

423
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
“This segment
is a test of heart and soul.”

424
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:13,000
You’re way off!

425
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Gon] Next time:
“A x Shocking x Tragedy”.

426
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
-Shocking!
-[Killua] Shocking?

427
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon and Killua] It’s a Shocker!
